cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use climval, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "climval: validation of climate model output against reference data"
abstract: >-
  climval is a Python library that validates climate model output against
  reference data. It aligns the two datasets in space, time and units
  (coordinates, longitude convention, regions, calendars, frequencies,
  regridding, unit conversion, paired missing values and cell-area weights),
  computes weighted metrics with xarray, lazily on dask arrays, records the
  provenance of every value, and gates continuous integration on thresholds
  with the climval check command and a GitHub Action.
